+[Remotion](https://www.remotion.dev/). It is made to be understood with the sound off: plain captions say what each
+beat shows ("Never know how to pose for photos?", "Poseit shows you how.", "Pick a pose to copy.", "Match the
+outline.", "It tells you what to fix.", "Hold still.", "It takes the photo for you.", "Here's your photo.", "99 poses
+for every kind of photo.", "Free for Android.", "Works offline.", "No account, no ads."), and a drawn generic phone
+shows the app's real screens. Real people come from free stock footage (Mixkit, credited in `CREDITS.md`); the app's
+own graphics on them (the live skeleton, the see-through lay figure, the per-limb colours, the score ring, the cue
+card, the countdown) are computed by the app's own pose model and matcher on that footage. The soundtrack is
+synthesized in Node. The plan is in `STORYBOARD.md`, the sound design in `sound-plan.md`, the caption and voice-over
+script in `vo.txt` (the same twelve sentences as `src/beats.ts` CAPTIONS), and the build notes (what is real, what was
+measured, what changed) in `NOTE.md`.
 
